# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows, where `core.autocrlf` would otherwise
# check the working tree out as CRLF. That makes `gofmt -l` flag files that CI
# accepts, because the pipeline on Linux checks out LF. A local formatting check
# would then not mean what the pipeline means, so pin LF for everything and let
# the two agree.
#
# No file here needs CRLF: the shell script must keep LF to run under `sh`, and
# there are no Windows batch or PowerShell scripts.
* text=auto eol=lf
